{#
  The confirmation email for a profile claim.

  Plain HTML in the same flat style as user/email_auth_code.html.twig — no
  layout, no CSS, no images. Mail clients strip most of it anyway, and a
  confirmation email that only makes sense with styling applied is a
  confirmation email that fails in Outlook's reading pane.

  The URL is printed as well as linked. Some clients do not linkify, some
  corporate gateways rewrite hrefs, and a visible URL can be copied by hand
  when both of those go wrong.
#}
<p>Dear {{ user.getDisplayName }},</p>

<p>
  Somebody using your account asked to claim the HMFP Search Tool profile for
  <strong>{{ physician.legalName }}{% if physician.credentials is not empty %}, {{ physician.credentials }}{% endif %}</strong>.
</p>

<p>If that was you, confirm it here and you will be asked for your NPI to finish:</p>

<p><a href="{{ confirmUrl }}">{{ confirmUrl }}</a></p>

{% if expiresAt %}
  <p>
    This link stops working on
    {{ expiresAt|date('l j F Y') }} at {{ expiresAt|date('g:i A') }}.
  </p>
{% endif %}

<p>
  Once the profile is linked to your account you will be able to propose changes
  to your biography and clinical interests. A data steward reviews anything you
  submit before it appears in the directory.
</p>

{#
  The line that matters. Somebody receiving this unexpectedly is the earliest
  and best signal that a claim is going to the wrong person — well before a
  steward sees it in a queue — so tell them plainly what to do about it.
#}
<p>
  <strong>If you did not ask for this, please do not use the link above.</strong>
  Email <a href="mailto:{{ supportEmail }}">{{ supportEmail }}</a> or call
  (617) 278-8162 and let us know, so we can find out who did.
</p>
